details.image_prompt:
{
  "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The two bowls of warm lemon custard are centered in the frame, arranged side-by-side with generous negative space. The camera angle is a 3/4 overhead view at 40 degrees, ensuring the creamy contents and fresh raspberries are clearly identifiable. Shallow depth of field with the nearest bowl in sharp focus and the second bowl slightly soft. The lighting is soft, natural side light from a window to the left, casting gentle shadows and creating a subtle, delicate sheen on the smooth surface of the custard. The scene is set on a worn, light-toned oak table with a slightly rumpled linen napkin underneath one bowl. A silver teaspoon rests casually beside one bowl, and a few scattered, bright red, textured fresh raspberries lie near the base of the plates. The custard is a pale, creamy yellow, appearing thick and silky with tiny, faint flecks of finely grated lemon zest visible throughout. Half of the fresh, vibrant raspberries are nestled into the custard, while others are piled naturally on top. One small, accidental droplet of custard sits on the rim of the left bowl. The atmosphere is warm, cozy, and inviting with a soft, natural color palette. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating—lived-in, warm, authentic. Not a sterile studio setup. Slight natural imperfections: an asymmetric garnish placement, a small custard drip on the plate rim, slightly uneven berry distribution. Include subtle traces of the cooking process: a few tiny granules of zest on the table. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image should be indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
}
